[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikeroySoft/factory/issues/comments/5622900146","html_url":"https://github.com/mikeroySoft/factory/issues/5#issuecomment-5622900146","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikeroySoft/factory/issues/5","id":5622900146,"node_id":"IC_kwDOUMiREs8AAAABTyalsg","user":{"login":"mikeroySoft","id":1791194,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTExOTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1791194?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft","html_url":"https://github.com/mikeroySoft","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-10T17:40:06Z","updated_at":"2026-09-10T17:40:06Z","body":"Triage: The issue is otherwise well-specified with a clear problem statement, file touches, and an exit gate with an observable done-condition (python -m unittest passes). However, there is a direct contradiction on a concrete implementation detail: the Scope section states the opt-in label is `needs-review`, while the Exit gate states the PR must have `factory-review`. Since this label name is used both in the feature behavior and in the acceptance test, the ambiguity would cause the verification test to fail depending on which is implemented, so it must be resolved before the issue is ready for an agent.\n\nQuestion: The Scope section says the opt-in label is `needs-review`, but the Exit gate says the PR must have `factory-review`. Which label name should the implementation and the acceptance test use?","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikeroySoft/factory/issues/comments/5622900146/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikeroySoft/factory/issues/comments/5622957847","html_url":"https://github.com/mikeroySoft/factory/issues/5#issuecomment-5622957847","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikeroySoft/factory/issues/5","id":5622957847,"node_id":"IC_kwDOUMiREs8AAAABTyeHFw","user":{"login":"mikeroySoft","id":1791194,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTExOTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1791194?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft","html_url":"https://github.com/mikeroySoft","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-10T17:44:46Z","updated_at":"2026-09-10T17:44:46Z","body":"Question: The Scope section says the opt-in label is needs-review, but the Exit gate says the PR must have factory-review. Which label name should the implementation and the acceptance test use?\n\nAnswer: use needs-review ","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikeroySoft/factory/issues/comments/5622957847/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikeroySoft/factory/issues/comments/5623439777","html_url":"https://github.com/mikeroySoft/factory/issues/5#issuecomment-5623439777","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikeroySoft/factory/issues/5","id":5623439777,"node_id":"IC_kwDOUMiREs8AAAABTy7hoQ","user":{"login":"mikeroySoft","id":1791194,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTExOTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1791194?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft","html_url":"https://github.com/mikeroySoft","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-10T18:23:46Z","updated_at":"2026-09-10T18:23:46Z","body":"Triage: The issue has a clear problem statement, specific file touches, and an observable done-condition (python -m unittest passes). The only blocker was a direct contradiction between the Scope section (opt-in label `needs-review`) and the Exit gate (label `factory-review`), which the maintainer flagged and the reporter resolved by answering 'use needs-review'. With that concrete implementation detail now unambiguous, the issue is fully specified and ready for an agent to implement.\n\nAgent brief: Extend `factory dispatch` with a review-only intake that discovers open, non-draft pull requests opted in via the `needs-review` label (the resolved label name, NOT `factory-review`) or a pending review request for the authenticated factory account. Record the PR number and current head SHA to avoid re-reviewing the same revision. The lane must accept ordinary contributor branches and must not require the `agent/<issue>` naming convention. Update the Exit gate text to reference `needs-review` for consistency. A test must prove that an open non-draft PR is selected when it has the `needs-review` label or requests the factory account, while drafts, closed PRs, unrelated review requests, and an already-recorded (PR, head SHA) pair are skipped. Verification: run `python -m unittest` and confirm it passes.","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikeroySoft/factory/issues/comments/5623439777/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikeroySoft/factory/issues/comments/5623718409","html_url":"https://github.com/mikeroySoft/factory/issues/5#issuecomment-5623718409","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikeroySoft/factory/issues/5","id":5623718409,"node_id":"IC_kwDOUMiREs8AAAABTzMiCQ","user":{"login":"mikeroySoft","id":1791194,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTExOTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1791194?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft","html_url":"https://github.com/mikeroySoft","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-10T18:43:16Z","updated_at":"2026-09-10T18:43:16Z","body":"Factory dispatcher escalating: PR #77: missing approval evidence bound to 6b577313fc468cfd20d96b0030c6ed099644352b; `factory-approved` label removed.\n\nEscalation packet: `/home/mike/dev/mikeroysoft/factory/.factory/escalations/5.md`\n\nWorker handoff notes:\n\n# Issue #5 handoff\n\n## Changed\n\n- Added review-only intake to normal dispatch before the manager consumes opt-in labels. Selects open, non-draft PRs carrying `needs-review` or a pending user review request matching the authenticated `gh api user` login (case-insensitive). Ordinary contributor branches are accepted; unrelated users and team requests are not opt-ins.\n- Records `review-intake` events with `pr` and `head` in `.factory/events.jsonl`; the shared PR/issue lock serializes deduplication and recording. Repeated dispatch skips recorded pairs. Dry runs write no state. Forced `--ticket` dispatch remains issue-only.\n- Reused the existing label, GitHub authentication, locks, and event journal. No configuration added. No review publication, contributor branch mutation, CI monitoring, or external merge behavior added.\n- Added the acceptance regression in tests/test_factory.py and updated existing dispatch fixtures. Added tests/__init__.py because plain `python -m unittest` previously discovered zero tests.\n- Updated README intake documentation and removed the obsolete manager message promising behavior when #5 lands. Corrected the local prompt's Exit gate label to `needs-review`; the prompt is not committed.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Acceptance regression failed before implementation and passed afterward.\n- Actual `python -m factory dispatch` CLI against a disposable repository and stub GitHub executable: pending-review contributor PR recorded once across two passes; dry run created no `.factory` directory.\n- `python -m unittest`: PASS, 178 tests, 4 skipped.\n- Focused dispatch integration checks: PASS, 8 tests.\n- Required `/home/mike/.local/share/uv/tools/factory/bin/python3 -m factory gate --report .factory/gate-report-5.md`: PASS (conflict-markers, test, leak-scan).\n\n## Commits\n\n- 45e8b03 — feat(dispatch): record opted-in pull request revisions\n- 6b57731 — test(dispatch): cover review intake in default unittest discovery\n\nBoth signed off with `git commit -s`. No push performed; no main updates or ticket closure.\n\n## Still unverified / next\n\n- Live GitHub discovery was not exercised; GitHub responses were simulated at the external boundary.\n- Four optional graphifyy history-extraction tests were skipped because graphifyy 0.9.56 is absent.\n- Intake follows the existing 1000-result list convention; repositories exceeding that open-PR window were not exercised.\n- Dispatcher can publish the branch PR and run its review/CI workflow. No further implementation is required for this ticket; publishing reviews and re-review execution remain out of scope.","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikeroySoft/factory/issues/comments/5623718409/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikeroySoft/factory/issues/comments/5626069868","html_url":"https://github.com/mikeroySoft/factory/issues/5#issuecomment-5626069868","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikeroySoft/factory/issues/5","id":5626069868,"node_id":"IC_kwDOUMiREs8AAAABT1cDbA","user":{"login":"mikeroySoft","id":1791194,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTExOTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1791194?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft","html_url":"https://github.com/mikeroySoft","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-10T22:05:47Z","updated_at":"2026-09-10T22:05:47Z","body":"Factory dispatcher escalating: review requested changes after manager FIX.\n\nEscalation packet: `/home/mike/dev/mikeroysoft/factory/.factory/escalations/5.md`\n\nWorker logs: `/home/mike/dev/mikeroysoft/factory/.factory/logs/5-attempt-2.log`\n\nWorker handoff notes:\n\n# Issue #5 handoff (attempt 2, FIX pass)\n\n## Outcome\n\nNo code change. The escalation was not a defect in the branch: it was missing\napproval evidence bound to head `6b577313fc468cfd20d96b0030c6ed099644352b`\n(`factory-approved` was removed). The manager FIX guidance said to preserve the\nexisting changes, avoid an empty commit, skip the optional review suggestions,\nand return the branch unchanged so the FIX pipeline can re-gate, push, and get a\nfresh APPROVE bound to the real PR head. I did exactly that.\n\n`agent/5` still points at `6b577313fc468cfd20d96b0030c6ed099644352b`, matches\n`origin/agent/5`, and the working tree is clean. No commits added, none amended,\nnothing pushed, no label restored, no approval check bypassed.\n\n## What the branch contains (unchanged from attempt 1)\n\n- `review_intake_pass` in `factory/dispatch.py`, run in normal dispatch after\n  `land_pass` and before `manage_pass` so the manager has not yet consumed the\n  opt-in label. Selects open, non-draft PRs carrying `needs-review`\n  (`LABEL_REVIEW`) or a pending user review request whose login case-folds equal\n  to the authenticated `gh api user` login, resolved lazily. Team requests carry\n  no `login` and never match. No branch-name constraint, so ordinary contributor\n  branches qualify.\n- Deduplication on `(PR number, head SHA)` via `review-intake` rows in\n  `.factory/events.jsonl` through the existing `record()`/journal writer. The\n  existing PR/issue-numbered `ticket_lock` serializes the read-then-append. Dry\n  runs take no lock, write no state, and only log.\n- Acceptance regression in `tests/test_factory.py` covering label opt-in, review\n  request opt-in, draft, closed, merged, unrelated request, wrong\n  `factory-review` label, a pre-recorded pair, and dedup across a second\n  `dispatch.main([])`.\n- `tests/__init__.py` so bare `python -m unittest` (the exit gate's literal\n  command) discovers the suite; the repo gate's `discover -s tests` is\n  unaffected and the marker is not shipped in the wheel.\n- README intake text and one stale `factory/manage.py` message that promised\n  behavior \"until #5 is implemented\".\n\n## Verification this pass\n\n- `python -m unittest`: PASS, 178 tests, 4 skipped (graphifyy 0.9.56 absent).\n- `/home/mike/.local/share/uv/tools/factory/bin/python3 -m factory gate --report .factory/gate-report-5.md`:\n  PASS (conflict-markers, test, leak-scan).\n- `git status`: clean, no divergence from `origin/agent/5`.\n\n## Still unverified / next\n\n- The blocker is entirely in the pipeline, not the code. Next step is a push and\n  a fresh review bound to the actual PR #77 head so `factory-approved` can be\n  reapplied by the normal path. If the head SHA the reviewer sees still does not\n  match the label evidence after that, the bug is in how the FIX pipeline binds\n  approval to a head, not in this branch.\n- Live GitHub discovery was never exercised; `gh` responses are simulated at the\n  external boundary in tests.\n- The `--limit 1000` open-PR window follows the existing list convention and was\n  not exercised beyond it.\n- The reviewer's optional suggestions were deliberately left alone per the FIX\n  guidance: `BlockingIOError` vs `OSError` idiom drift at\n  `factory/dispatch.py:224`, the per-PR re-read of `events.jsonl`, the\n  `--limit 1000` inconsistency with `merge_pass_locked`, and absent\n  `execution.resource` telemetry around the intake lock. All are judgement calls\n  with no behavior consequence here; fold them into a later cleanup if the repo\n  wants one idiom.","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikeroySoft/factory/issues/comments/5626069868/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]